    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jose Caballero** (80.26) and **Corbin Carroll** (79.53) anchor our production, standing as the clear-cut priority starts. **Jose Caballero** benefits from a massive 18% boost due to a favorable matchup against Abbott, while his aggressive base-running profile aligns perfectly with our organizational emphasis on SB. Simultaneously, **Corbin Carroll** is primed for a high-ceiling performance against Taj Bradley; the combination of a positive park factor and a slow pitcher delivery window creates an elite environment for him to exploit the stolen base category, which remains our primary efficiency driver. **Tyler Soderstrom** (72.72) and **Seiya Suzuki** (72.58) also rate as high-confidence starts, with both players seeing significant score inflation from favorable park factors and platoon advantages against Ure\u00f1a and Corbin, respectively.\n\nWe continue to track several \"Lineup Pending\" designations, specifically for **Gabriel Moreno** and **Travis Bazzana**, though their projected roles remain strong enough to justify inclusion. The most difficult bench decision involved **Zach McKinstry**, who narrowly missed the cut with a 42.06 score. While his platoon edge against Newcomb was intriguing, the optimizer ultimately pivoted away from him in favor of higher-floor options like **Austin Riley**, whose base profile remains more stable despite a tougher matchup against Harrison. We are closely monitoring the weather, as the wind-out conditions in the **Dalton Rushing** and **Alex Freeland** matchups provide a marginal cushion for their otherwise middling projected efficiency, but we advise caution regarding the 3.45 xERA of the opposing pitcher facing **Austin Riley**. **Mickey Moniak** remains held in reserve on the IL, and while we keep an eye on depth pieces like **Cole Young** and **Kyle Karros**, they lack the necessary situational upside to crack the current lineup given the strength of our primary starters.",
